WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.292 --> 00:00:01.793
Say it. I deserve it.

00:00:01.877 --> 00:00:02.794
I deserve it.

00:00:02.878 --> 00:00:03.629
Again.

00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:05.464
-I deserve it.
-I deserve it.

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:06.840
Feels good, doesn't it?

00:00:11.178 --> 00:00:15.265
Shrink Next Door tells the story
of a very co-dependent relationship

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:17.017
that spans 27 years.

00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:19.853
Marty Markowitz and his sister Phyllis,

00:00:19.937 --> 00:00:21.438
they've just lost their parents.

00:00:21.772 --> 00:00:23.106
He's very vulnerable

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:26.026
and feels that the walls are
caving in on him.

00:00:26.944 --> 00:00:28.111
Marty, what are you doing?

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:31.740
Seeing how much stress
her big brother was under,

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:34.743
Phyllis recommended a therapist, Ike.

00:00:35.536 --> 00:00:38.956
At first, Dr. Ike is everything
you would hope a therapist would be,

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:42.042
a great listener, really helps him
solve problems.

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:43.502
The thing about obstacles,

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:46.046
they're either stumbling blocks
or stepping stones.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:48.632
They're kind of having an identity crisis.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:52.594
Ike is feeling a lack of fulfillment
with being a therapist.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.514
And Marty is really ill-equipped

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:58.100
to deal with the obstacles
that are being thrown his way.

00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:59.601
-You ok, buddy?
-Yeah.

00:00:59.685 --> 00:01:01.979
Having one of my panic attacks.
It'll pass.

00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:05.357
Ike helped him enormously
at the beginning,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.236
then that relationship
morphed into something unhealthy.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:10.362
Welcome!

00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:12.322
Dr. Ike starts to manipulate him.

00:01:12.406 --> 00:01:14.783
He takes over Marty's Hamptons house.

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:17.619
What's the big deal
if they think it's my place, huh?

00:01:17.703 --> 00:01:20.622
-I mean, who cares whose place it is?
-I agree.

00:01:20.706 --> 00:01:23.584
This doctor seems
a little unconventional, huh?

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.670
But the thing is, he cares so much.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:30.340
It starts to get further away
from what's acceptable.

00:01:30.424 --> 00:01:32.176
You know, sometimes I feel like
I'm working on you,

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:33.594
but I don't think you're working on you.

00:01:33.677 --> 00:01:35.762
I promise. I'll work harder.

00:01:35.846 --> 00:01:38.473
Marty doesn't realize how bad it is.

00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:42.227
He's just thankful that
this therapist is in his corner.

00:01:42.311 --> 00:01:44.813
-I don't trust him.
-He's trying to help me.

00:01:45.314 --> 00:01:46.648
Phyllis was toxic.

00:01:46.732 --> 00:01:49.443
You did the right thing
by cutting her out of your life.

00:01:51.028 --> 00:01:52.863
By separating him from Phyllis,

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.949
Marty and Ike
really become so intertwined,

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.784
which is the heart of the story.

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.578
You are growing, Marty!

00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:00.829
I mean, this is all because of you.

00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:03.290
You should be proud of yourself.
I'm proud of you.

00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:07.044
I wanted the audience to feel
sort of seduced and charmed by Ike,

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.337
just as Marty is.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:11.757
Everything's gonna be all right.
I'm not gonna let anyone use you.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.674
It's heartbreaking.

00:02:12.758 --> 00:02:15.636
You go into it thinking,
"Well, that would never happen to me.

00:02:15.761 --> 00:02:18.889
I'd be impervious to the journey
that this guy went on."

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:21.475
When you're in it,
you just think differently.

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:24.186
It's very easy to believe
what we wanna believe.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.480
You know I'm doing this for you.

00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:30.776
Anyone at any moment, feeling vulnerable,
could go down this road.

00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:33.403
Trust is at the very core of who I am.

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:34.780
I do trust you.

